diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index c676109..9ec8a3c 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@ Use [Holzmann's original ten rules](https://spinroot.com/gerard/pdf/P10.pdf) as
 | 9 | Restrict pointer indirection; no concealed dereferences or function pointers. |
 | 10 | Strict warnings without warnings and regular static analysis. |
 
+Rule 5 has two published formulations: the 2006 paper and [overview](https://spinroot.com/p10/) use an average, while the author's [detailed Rule 5](https://spinroot.com/p10/rule5.html) uses N assertions in functions longer than M lines, with N=2/M=20 for safety-critical code. Following the user's 2026-10-01 choice, retain the project's strict N=2/M=20 gate and also report any global density with an explicit denominator and counting limitations. The historical per-function findings are valid strict-gate findings, not by themselves proof of violating the paper's average. Never use an average to excuse a missing safety-critical contract or manufacture assertions to meet either formulation.
+
 The existing checker is a project gate, not a complete proof of these rules. Preserve its original thresholds, source coverage and failure expectations. In particular, its Rule 5 requirement of two assertions in functions over 20 code lines differs from the original average across functions; typed-object non-null/alignment counting does not prove useful assertion density. Its direct-recursion/text-pattern checks do not establish an acyclic whole-program call graph, finite `for` bounds, minimum data scope, every checked return, or all header/macro/pointer semantics. Review those separately and record unresolved items as FAIL or NOT PROVEN, never PASS.
 
 Known project policies also differ from strict original compliance: the checker forbids allocation even during initialization, excludes third-party middleware, permits its named permanent task/fault loops, selected protocol/estimator conditionals and the exact FreeRTOS idle-hook double-pointer outputs. The existing [coding standard](docs/FCCG/platform/details/CODING_STANDARD.md) also records fixed task entry pointers passed directly to `xTaskCreateStatic()`; this does not authorize a runtime callback registry or further pointer indirection. Do not enlarge these exceptions without explicit authorization. Maintain upstream licenses and version provenance. Inventory linked third-party code (including HAL, RTOS, libraries and callbacks), document each controlled exception and its consequences for recursion, stack and timing analysis; do not erase its violations or claim whole-firmware original compliance from a first-party gate alone. Host fault-injection harnesses may intercept the terminal trap using setjmp/longjmp; this test-only mechanism must never enter target firmware or be reported as MCU recovery.
